      ":question/id": "b43704d0-6be6-52a5-b0ab-6873dc76da8f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=8 x^{4} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}+9 x \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{y^{3}}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(8 x^{4} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}+9 x \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{y^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(8 x^{4} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)})+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(9 x \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{3 x^{2}}{y^{3}}) \\\\  & =8 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\sin{\\left(y \\right)})+9 x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\arctan{\\left(y \\right)})-3 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{1}{y^{3}}) \\\\  & =8 x^{4}\\cdot \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+9 x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y^{2} + 1}-3 x^{2}\\cdot (- \\frac{3}{y^{4}}) \\\\  & =8 x^{4} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{4}} + \\frac{9 x}{y^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
