      ":question/problem": "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=9 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}+6 x e^{y}- \\frac{6 x^{2}}{y^{4}}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(9 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}+6 x e^{y}- \\frac{6 x^{2}}{y^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(9 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(6 x e^{y})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{6 x^{2}}{y^{4}}) \\\\  & =9 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\ln{\\left(y \\right)})+6 x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(e^{y})-6 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{1}{y^{4}}) \\\\  & =9 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+6 x\\cdot e^{y}-6 x^{2}\\cdot (- \\frac{4}{y^{5}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{24 x^{2}}{y^{5}} + 6 x e^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
